  "description": "The **user** resource (plural\u202f*users*) supports full creation, single\u2011record lookup, bulk read, and updates, while deletion is deliberately disabled. Pagination is turned on by default, serving pages that start at number\u202f0 and contain 20 entries each unless overridden.\n\nEach user record consists of an **id** (a non\u2011nullable integer) and an **email** (a non\u2011nullable string). The **name** field is a simple string, and **age** is an integer that may be null; if omitted, it defaults to \u201c0\u201d. System\u2011generated metadata includes a **created_by** string and optional **notes**, which are nullable strings. The resource is linked to a **profile** in a one\u2011to\u2011one relationship where the user acts as the host, and it also has a one\u2011to\u2011many relationship to **posts**. Built\u2011in timestamps for **created_at** and **updated_at** are both enabled."
